@spec status_edit_spec  src=tests/specs/status_edit_spec.lua  loc=249  cases=11
@harness   mk

# Intent
  Chrome-level pin for the status bar's editable cells: a segment carrying `set` draws as a
  control rather than text, and both routes into it — the wheel and the InputText — commit
  through `set` clamped to the declared range. Real chrome over a fake imgui; recipe from
  picker_create_spec, with the item, wheel and cursor calls a cell makes added.

# Helpers
  @fn mkChrome(h)  @ 51-54
  @fn mkBar(harness, value, edit)  @ 57-67
      -- A one-cell bar over a value the test can watch. `edit` selects the number behaviour.
  @fn mkFlags(harness)  @ 72-85

# Cases
  @case 'the wheel over a number cell steps by `step` and stops at the declared bounds'  [harness]  @ 89-101
  @case 'part notches accumulate; the wheel only steps on a whole one'  [harness]  @ 105-114
  @case 'step='x2' doubles and halves rather than adding'  [harness]  @ 118-130
  @case 'a display-only cell claims no hit rect; an editable one does'  [harness]  @ 134-144
  @case 'a cell's declared width is its value box; the label sits to its left'  [harness]  @ 148-156
  @case 'a click opens the edit; Enter commits the typed value, clamped'  [harness]  @ 160-172
  @case 'Esc leaves the value alone and closes the edit'  [harness]  @ 176-186
  @case 'a click on a flag token flips that flag and leaves its neighbours alone'  [harness]  @ 190-201
  @case 'each flag token claims its own hit rect, sized to its own label'  [harness]  @ 205-217
  @case 'a flags cell's recorded rect spans every token and the gaps between them'  [harness]  @ 221-231
  @case 'a lit token has the footprint of an unlit one, so toggling never reflows the row'  [harness]  @ 235-247

